  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on which lottery is more right-skewed, which in this case is Lottery A (90% chance of loss). The individual, however, chooses based on the higher probability of avoiding a loss (i.e., 55% in B), which reflects a preference for a *less* right-skewed lottery. The information considered by the individual (chance of losing nothing) is partially related to skewness but is not equivalent — they focus only on the best outcome’s probability, not the overall distribution asymmetry. Their justification aligns with risk aversion or minimizing loss probability, not with preferring more right-skewed distributions. There is no indication that they evaluated or preferred the lottery with greater probability mass on unfavorable outcomes. In fact, they do the opposite. Therefore, the decision reason (preferring more right-skewed lottery) was not used.",
